From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restyle only structurally affected siblings on child
 insertion

Every insertion stamped restyle_subtree() on the new parent, so prepending one marker
span to each list item recascaded every list subtree. Like Gecko's RestyleForInsertOrChange,
restyle the inserted children, and use the parent's selector flags to restyle only the
edge children or later siblings that structural selectors can match. :empty, from-end
selectors, sibling-index(), slots and shadow hosts keep the whole-parent restyle; :has()
keeps its own invalidator.
---
 src/mutator.rs | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 76 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index a85e9ab..9819b58 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -20,6 +20,23 @@ use thin_vec::ThinVec;

 const TEMPLATE_CONTENTS_FRAGMENT_NAME: &str = "#document-fragment";

+/// Whether inserting a child must recascade the parent's whole subtree: its own `:empty`, a
+/// `:last-child`-style or `sibling-index()` dependency on every child, or a flat tree that
+/// slotting reshapes. Anything else goes through `restyle_for_insertion`.
+fn insertion_restyles_whole_parent(parent: &Node) -> bool {
+    use selectors::matching::ElementSelectorFlags;
+
+    if !parent.is_element() || parent.is_slot_element() || parent.attached_shadow_root_id().is_some()
+    {
+        return true;
+    }
+    parent.selector_flags().get().intersects(
+        ElementSelectorFlags::HAS_EMPTY_SELECTOR
+            | ElementSelectorFlags::HAS_SLOW_SELECTOR
+            | ElementSelectorFlags::MAY_HAVE_TREE_COUNTING_FUNCTION,
+    )
+}
